    "explanation": "TRP-00311, Jurong East MRT to Buona Vista MRT, 13 August 2026. The GPS trace EV-GPS-00311 records 12.4 km against a booked optimal route of 7.5 km (EV-TRIP-00311) — an excess of 4.9 km, or 65.3% of optimal. That passes both POL-RD-01 tests (more than 0.8 km in absolute terms and more than 20% of optimal) and is a material deviation (over 50%).\n\nNo clause excuses it. The only traffic advisory for this trip (EV-ADVIS-00311-01) is missing with weight 0.0, so POL-RD-03 cannot be run and POL-RD-13 gives any external-traffic explanation no weight; no party cited that missing identifier as an exculpatory record, so POL-RD-10(5) is not engaged by it. The driver's account that the rider asked for Clementi does not exonerate anything: the rider's chat message of 16:06:05 (EV-CHAT-00311) does name The Clementi Mall, but the nearest the vehicle came to that waypoint was 2,595 m against the 200 m POL-RD-04 requires, so under POL-RD-04 and POL-RD-14 the request did not cause the excess and no distance is excluded. The driver's further statement that the rider said 'never mind go straight' is not in the complete two-message chat export and carries no weight. There was no pickup or dropoff amendment (POL-RD-05 cannot be run), and the vehicle type is RYDE_X, not a pooled trip (POL-RD-12 does not apply). The rider's 'Bukit Timah' and '7 km' characterisations are not established by any admitted artifact and do not change the measured excess.\n\nMoney. The fare is metered; the surge multiplier read from EV-FARE-00311 is 1.00. recomputed_fare = (3.80 base + 0.75 x 7.5 km + 0.28 x 12.0 min) x 1.00 + 0.80 platform fee = 13.585. charged_total = 20.62. The policy refund is 20.62 - 13.585 = 7.035, rounded up to 7.05. That is 34.1% of the fare — above the 0.50 de minimis and below the 90% that would convert it to a full refund. Because the rider put SGD 5.00 in issue, the amount returned to her is capped at that SGD 5.00.\n\nThe driver's no-pattern point is accepted: driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 over 260 completed trips, so POL-RD-06 is not established, and there is neither a full-refund uplift nor a driver-conduct referral. There are no ERP, toll or surcharge lines, so POL-RD-09 makes no correction and no billing-integrity referral arises. Billed distance (12.4 km) matches the trace, so no unbilled-kilometre compensation is due to the driver. The trace is unimpaired (145 fixes, 10-second cadence, no gaps), so POL-RD-07 and the escalation trigger POL-RD-10(3) are not engaged and no escalation is required. The monetary effect (SGD 5.00) is below the SGD 8.00 automatic-execution threshold, so this refund is executed on issue."
