    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "To the rider and the driver, on trip TRP-00311 (Jurong East to Buona Vista, 13 Aug 2026).\n\nThe deviation is established. The GPS trace (EV-GPS-00311) records 12.4 km against the platform's booked optimal of 7.5 km on the AYE — an excess of 4.9 km, or 65.3% of optimal. Both POL-RD-01 tests pass (greater than 0.8 km and greater than 20%), so the deviation is established; at over 50% of optimal it is also a MATERIAL deviation. The trace is clean for policy purposes — 145 fixes at a 10-second cadence, 100% coverage, no gaps — so POL-RD-07 (a)–(c) is not engaged and the finding may rest on the trace alone.\n\nThe driver's account does not reduce the excess. The chat log (EV-CHAT-00311) shows the rider did ask to stop at The Clementi Mall at 16:06:05 and the driver answered 'ok' at 16:06:35, but the trace never approaches the requested waypoint: the nearest fix is 2,595 m away, against the 200 m corroboration threshold POL-RD-04 sets, and within_threshold is false. Under POL-RD-14, an instruction that was given but not followed excludes no distance, so the excess stands as measured. The driver's further account — that the rider said 'never mind, go straight' — appears nowhere in the two-message export. No traffic advisory covers this trip's window (EV-ADVIS-00311-01 is MISSING, weight 0.0), so no external traffic cause excuses any part of the excess (POL-RD-13, POL-RD-03 unavailable), and no amendment or pooled-itinerary adjustment applies (POL-RD-05, POL-RD-12).\n\nMoney, read from the fare breakdown's money block (EV-FARE-00311): charged total SGD 20.62; recomputed fare under POL-RD-02 = (3.80 base + 0.75 x 7.5 km + 0.28 x 12.0 min) x the surge multiplier of 1.00 recorded on EV-FARE-00311 + 0.80 platform fee = SGD 13.585; refund = 20.62 - 13.585 = SGD 7.035, rounded up to SGD 7.05. That is 34.1% of the charge — below the 90% that would make it a full refund — and above the SGD 0.50 de minimis, so the outcome is a partial refund of SGD 7.05.\n\nThe driver argued that the refund is capped at the SGD 5.00 recorded as the contested amount. I have not accepted that. POL-RD-02 fixes the refund arithmetically as the difference between what was charged and the fare that should have been charged, and the money block records the payable at SGD 7.05. The SGD 5.00 is the sum the rider put in issue; it does not limit the correction of the fare.\n\nNo repeat-deviation pattern is established (0 deviation flags in 90 days on 260 completed trips), so no full-refund uplift and no driver-conduct referral follow (POL-RD-06). There is no billing-integrity defect — no ERP gantries, no tolls and no surcharge were charged — so POL-RD-09(4) produces no referral. Profile counters that the clauses do not name were treated as context only, as POL-GEN-01 requires. The monetary effect, SGD 7.05, is below the SGD 8.00 execution threshold, so this provisional ruling is executed automatically; either party may appeal under POL-GEN-04."
